 {"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:49:26.126767Z","id":"bae67ed2481f42d62209eeb476767341fac23b908bcd76209138ced8178e6ee8","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"eb75126a93fa8854cf3f7bce204b1decc9c17b2b625e416c92506d54e0ab8bd0","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
