+{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T19:08:07.498281Z","id":"0d487e12fbf96d41f05b36bab2a3ac94a62f0f2df52469f9d0d082acdac8edfa","body":{"detail":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"CALLER_CWD is the directory a projection is resumed in, not a stand-in for a defect: the caller's cwd is the contract for codex, pi, copilot and gemini","supersedes":"98ef9cbd37b7cc86dbbbba1ab5969dda5ff3c2db9956c86b6664bf989d8390aa","tags":["goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
